From dab02eba6811506f68f6ce0751f0ddc4a2982dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): external-run cards, review round 2: poll bound
 to its park, terminal recovery clears the outage, shell Retry-After delays
 the probe [daveey]

Review 5991116946 of PR #3745 at 3c8f438b found three behaviour defects. Each is red on 3c8f438b with the
reviewer's repro (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_external_review2.py starts from that file) and green here.

1. An old CI response woke a replacement park. The sweep captured the park id in `_due` but `_record_watch`
   reloaded the latest park and `apply_poll` checked only `status == scheduled`. A card woken and parked again
   while the GitHub read was in flight took the old run's result. `apply_poll` now takes the `park_id` and `ref`
   the poll was read for and checks both inside its write transaction, before recording, asserting or clearing
   a blocker, or waking. Covered for a replacement on another run and for a new park on the same ref.
2. A healthy read whose job had finished returned before `_clear_blocker`, so an outage whose first recovery
   read was a finished run stayed open with no scheduled card left to clear it. The blocker is now cleared on
   any ok/degraded read before the terminal wake. Covered for a succeeded and a failed job.
3. A shell probe's `HERMES_WATCH {"service":"rate_limited","retry_after":N}` delayed only the displayed record:
   `task_wake_checks.next_at` stayed at now + every. `note_probe` now returns the delay and `_after_probe` uses
   max(every, delay). The generation is untouched and an in-flight expedite (next_at moved before the claim's
   slot) still wins. `retry_after` is ignored unless the service is rate_limited and never shortens the cadence.

Proof: 11 tests in test_kanban_external_review2.py; 4 reviewer cases red on 3c8f438b, all green now. Seven
mutants (park-id check, ref check, missing-park check, terminal clear, rate_limited condition, max(every, delay),
expedite branch) each fail at least one test.
